{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "vector": "identity-approval-cases.phone",
  "source": {
    "checkout": "bf4075b0a2e8092b04b726c59a7b085d5a37e6f6",
    "note": "phoneDSH-only /identity and /approval body vector; no dsh-bot upstream file exists. The checkout records the pinned upstream batch this contract sits beside, not the origin of these cases."
  },
  "upstream": [],
  "delta": [
    "P05/P26: /identity/register uses the App-issued dshg_ token, never the body sessionId; missing/empty/unknown/revoked/expired/foreign tokens are one unauthorized answer, and a body argsDigest mismatch is argument digest mismatch. Success is {ok:true,id}; the id is the registration cancelled by /identity/cancel.",
    "P05/P26: /approval validation order and exact refusals are frozen: unattributed, stale:digest_mismatch, stale:command_mismatch, stale:sandbox_effect, stale:always_scope; the expected scope is until for a known effect and session for all-unknown effects, none is accepted as a one-shot override, and sandbox escalation requires none.",
    "P05/P26: an always decision stores a standing grant only when every effect can use one (`canUseStandingGrant`: known, and external-send or an explicit grant resource). Destructive operations and every tool.unclassified effect (known false) have alwaysScope none on their card and resolve always to a consumed one-shot: the response carries approvalDecision always with scope once, and the user is asked again next time (PC-20261113-approval-scope-and-haptics; PC-20261114-approval-once-scope in mcp-endpoint.md section 8.4).",
    "P05/P26: approval outcomes carry pending plus optional approvalId/message/expiresAt/approvalDecision/scope; interactive card timeout is 300000 ms and a durable todo expires after 24 h. A /identity/cancel of a registration closes its interactive approvals with approval cancelled."
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "approvalTimeoutMs": 300000,
    "approvalExpiryMs": 86400000
  },
